# `make deb` provides both (docs/26#releases).

Package: fjarr-setup
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Replaces: fjarr-agent (<< 0.1.3~)
Description: Fjarr setup tool
 What `fjarr-agent setup`, `net`, `drivers` and `display` run, and the
 command fjarr-setup for a host with no agent: the desktop host of a robot
 whose agent runs in a container (`fjarr-setup setup desktop --container`).

Package: fjarr-agent
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, fjarr-setup (= ${binary:Version}),
 gstreamer1.0-plugins-base, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good, gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad,
 gstreamer1.0-nice, gstreamer1.0-plugins-base-apps, glib-networking
Recommends: mesa-va-drivers | intel-media-va-driver, fjarr-tools
Description: Fjarr agent: peer-to-peer connectivity for robots
 Streams cameras and the desktop, gives operators a terminal and a network
 link, over WebRTC. Runs as its own unprivileged account. The service starts
 once /etc/fjarr/fjarr.toml exists; `fjarr-agent setup` writes it.

Package: libfjarr-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, pkgconf,
 libgstreamer1.0-dev, libgstreamer-plugins-base1.0-dev, libgstreamer-plugins-bad1.0-dev,
 libsoup-3.0-dev, libsystemd-dev, nlohmann-json3-dev, libtomlplusplus-dev, libnice-dev
Description: Fjarr robot library: static library, headers and CMake package
 For robot software that embeds Fjarr: find_package(fjarr) and link
 fjarr::fjarr. Static in 0.x, until the ABI is stable (docs/26).

Package: fjarr-tools
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libcap2-bin
Description: Fjarr operator tools: fjarr-connect
 fjarr-connect is the native operator client: a network link to a robot
 (given cap_net_admin at install) and `fjarr-connect shell`, the robot's
 terminal in yours.

Package: fjarr-desktop-session
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, fjarr-setup (= ${binary:Version})
Recommends: gdm3, gnome-shell
Replaces: fjarr-desktop-wayland (<< 0.1.3~)
Description: Fjarr remote desktop, the GNOME session's side
 fjarr-desktop-session runs in the desktop account's session and hands the
 agent a PipeWire connection narrowed to the screen and an input socket; the
 fjarr-desktop group and the GDM watchdog come with it. No agent: on a robot
 fjarr-desktop-wayland brings this package, and on the host of a robot whose
 agent runs in a container it is installed alone. Nothing is switched on at
 install: `setup desktop` does that, and `--undo desktop` reverses it.

Package: fjarr-desktop-wayland
Architecture: any
# libpipewire-0.3-modules: the client modules the package's own PipeWire configuration loads
# (packaging/pipewire/fjarr-pipewire-client.conf), so neither pipewire-bin nor its client.conf is needed.
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, fjarr-agent (= ${binary:Version}), libpipewire-0.3-modules
Recommends: fjarr-desktop-session (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Fjarr remote desktop for GNOME on Wayland
 The robot's screen as a video track, and the operator's pointer and keyboard
 on it, through mutter, in the agent's own account. The session's side is
 fjarr-desktop-session, which apt installs with this package. Nothing is
 switched on at install: `fjarr-agent setup desktop` does that.

Package: fjarr-desktop-x11
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, fjarr-agent (= ${binary:Version}), gstreamer1.0-x
Description: Fjarr remote desktop for X11 kiosks
 The robot's screen as a video track per monitor, and the operator's pointer
 and keyboard on it, through the X server: ximagesrc, XTest and XFixes from
 the agent's own process. fjarr-x11-session runs in the kiosk session, grants
 the agent's account (xhost +si:localuser:fjarr) and keeps the outputs laid
 out. Nothing is switched on at install: `fjarr-agent setup desktop` links the
 session's autostart entry, and `--undo desktop` removes it.
